title: I am unsure whether Emacs's echo area is the right place when a save hides many things.
pid: 4198866b-539c-4131-8003-a02f4084c339
body: |2-
  Each line is a sentence with up to three titles; Jeff's titles are
  long, so five hides make a tall echo area that the next message
  erases. A buffer, as warnings get, would keep them. I chose the echo
  area for brevity, as the mission asked.
